factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  The reel_script says the project report was prepared for the 'textile technology centre' and that SIMA gave the report 'to the government' — roughly consistent, but the reel_script's claim that SIMA 'gave the report' is fine; however the caption states the centre 'will be set up' with Rs 10 crore, which the article supports.
  The reel_script and caption describe Damodaran as the 'joint secretary' of the Southern India Banian Manufacturers Association, but the article gives the full name as 'தென்னிந்திய பனியன் உற்பத்தியாளர் சங்க (சைமா) இணை செயலாளர்' — this matches, so no problem here.
  The reel_script says 'Tiruppur ... Rs 45,000 crore in knitwear exports' and the slides say 'Tiruppur export annual Rs 45,000 crore' — matches the article.
  The caption's description 'சீனா இத்துறையில் முன்னேறி வருவதால் ஒருங்கிணைந்த ஆராய்ச்சி மையம் அமைக்க சைமா அரசிடம் விரிவான அறிக்கை அளித்தது' mixes two facts into one sentence: the article says China is advancing and separately that SIMA gave the report; the causal link ('since China is advancing, SIMA submitted the report') is not stated in the article.
  The reel_script states 'இதையடுத்து ஒருங்கிணைந்த ஆராய்ச்சி மையம் அமைக்க சைமா அரசிடம் விரிவான அறிக்கை அளித்தது' ('following this, SIMA submitted a detailed report'), introducing a sequence/cause that the article does not state.
